cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this reproducibility benchmark, please cite both this package and the original CIC-MalMem-2022 dataset/paper."
title: "CIC-MalMem-2022 Enriched Leakage-Audited Reproducibility Benchmark"
version: "0.1.2"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: "Ibrahim"
    given-names: "Ahmed Ibrahim Lotfy Abdo"
    affiliation: "Department of Computer Science, Military Technical College, Cairo, Egypt"

date-released: "2026-09-12"
repository-code: "https://github.com/AhmedLotfy9513/malmem-leakage-aware-benchmark"
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22726638"
abstract: >
  An enriched, leakage-audited, explainability- and ATT&CK-aligned
  reproducibility benchmark derived from CIC-MalMem-2022. The package
  includes leakage-aware split manifests, benchmark protocols,
  explainability artifacts, counterfactual and stability analyses,
  evidence-aware MITRE ATT&CK alignment artifacts, statistical summaries,
  and machine-verifiable integrity checks.
keywords:
  - malware
  - memory forensics
  - CIC-MalMem-2022
  - machine learning
  - explainable AI
  - SHAP
  - counterfactual explanations
  - MITRE ATT&CK
  - reproducibility

doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22726638"
